## Summary Table: Why Mastery is Mandatory

| Chapter | The Exam Focus | The Real-World Danger of Failure |
|---|---|---|
| 1. Chemistry & Physics | Fume classes and detonation velocity | Toxic gas poisoning or structural collapse |
| 2. Initiation Systems | Delay timing patterns (milliseconds) | High vibrations that crack neighboring house foundations |
| 3. Blast Geometry | Burden, spacing, and powder factor calculations | Dangerous flyrock projectiles or poor rock breakage |
| 4. Product Selection | Water resistance and density of ANFO vs. Emulsions | Misfires due to dissolved or degraded product |
| 5. Safety Protocols | Guarding, signals, and clearing misfires | Accidental detonations and fatal site injuries |
| 6. Legal & Storage | Magazine rules and inventory logs | License revocation, theft, or spontaneous storage fires |

